From d882b931bf423f5472f83e59b22eaab8236e6dba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port <port@local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:11:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/32] remoteproc: qcom: add ADSP loader compatibility driver

Qualcomm Android userspace on SM6225 starts the ADSP by writing to
/sys/kernel/boot_adsp/boot rather than the generic remoteproc state
file. The shipping PAS resource keeps auto_boot disabled, so an
upstream PAS node alone leaves that init contract unserved.

Add a small qcom,adsp-loader platform driver that resolves the
remoteproc from qcom,rproc-handle, exposes the vendor boot/ssr
write-only files, and delegates lifecycle to
rproc_boot()/rproc_shutdown(). The loader owns exactly one
remoteproc power reference, avoiding repeated boot writes changing
the core refcount.

Carry the optional adsp_variant firmware selection. Apply a selected
name with rproc_set_firmware() only when it is a complete .mdt/.mbn
file name. Bare stems such as Khaje adsp2 keep the remoteproc
default, matching the effective downstream behaviour and avoiding
an invented firmware file name.

This does not implement the vendor SPF readiness check; Q6APM/Q6PRM
clients use the normal AudioReach/PDR path. Add the binding and ABI
documentation. Compile-tested only; not verified on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Port <port@local>
